!!! Middleware: what happens to every request and every response.
!!!
!!! Not a chain of wrapped callables. Matrix has no capturing closures, so the
!!! `next(request)` shape that every other framework uses cannot be written —
!!! there is nothing to capture `next` in. What replaces it is two lists: one
!!! of checks that run before a handler and may answer instead of it, and one
!!! of changes applied to whatever response comes back.
!!!
!!! That is less general. A middleware cannot run code on the way out that
!!! depends on a local it set on the way in, and it cannot wrap a handler in
!!! an `attempt`. What it is instead is explicit: the whole of what happens
!!! around a handler is two arrays you can print.
!!!
!!! Both lists name their behaviour with text, for the same reason routes name
!!! handlers with text. See nilweb.routing.router for the long version.

book nilweb.middleware.chain

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.text
read everything from nilweb.text.scan
read everything from nilweb.http.method
read everything from nilweb.http.status
read everything from nilweb.http.headers
read everything from nilweb.http.request
read everything from nilweb.http.response


!!! --- A check that runs before the handler.
!!!
!!! `setting` is the one argument the check needs — the allowed origin, the
!!! realm, the byte ceiling. One argument rather than a general bag because
!!! every check here wants exactly none or one, and a bag would be a map that
!!! Matrix cannot index anyway.

public guard begin record
    field kind as text
    field setting as text
end record


!!! --- A change applied to the response on the way out.

public finisher begin record
    field kind as text
    field setting as text
end record


public chain begin record
    field guards as array of guard
    field finishers as array of finisher
end record


public new-chain returns chain begin paragraph
    variable guards as array of guard is []
    variable finishers as array of finisher is []
    give build chain with guards being guards, finishers being finishers
end paragraph


public with-guard receives one-chain as chain, kind as text, setting as text returns chain begin paragraph
    variable guards as array of guard is []
    repeat for each existing in one-chain.guards
        append existing to guards
    end repeat
    append build guard with kind being kind, setting being setting to guards
    give build chain with guards being guards, finishers being one-chain.finishers
end paragraph


public with-finisher receives one-chain as chain, kind as text, setting as text returns chain begin paragraph
    variable finishers as array of finisher is []
    repeat for each existing in one-chain.finishers
        append existing to finishers
    end repeat
    append build finisher with kind being kind, setting being setting to finishers
    give build chain with guards being one-chain.guards, finishers being finishers
end paragraph


!!! --- The outcome of running the guards.
!!! `stopped` true means the response is the answer and the handler must not run.

public guard-result begin record
    field stopped as boolean
    field response as http-response
end record


!!! --- Run every guard in order. The first to object answers.

public run-guards receives one-chain as chain, request as http-request returns guard-result begin paragraph
    repeat for each each-guard in one-chain.guards
        value verdict is run-one-guard with the-guard being each-guard, request being request
        when verdict.stopped then
            give verdict
        end when
    end repeat
    give build guard-result with stopped being false, response being (empty-response with code being status-ok)
end paragraph


run-one-guard receives the-guard as guard, request as http-request returns guard-result begin paragraph
    give switch the-guard.kind
        case "require-host" then
            stop switching with (require-host with request being request)
        case "body-limit" then
            stop switching with (body-limit with request being request, setting being the-guard.setting)
        case "require-form" then
            stop switching with (require-form with request being request)
        case "block-method" then
            stop switching with (block-method with request being request, setting being the-guard.setting)
        otherwise
            !!! A guard nobody wired is a configuration mistake, and a
            !!! configuration mistake in a security check must fail closed.
            stop switching with (stopped-with with response being
                (error-response with code being status-internal-error,
                    explanation being "No guard is wired for the name " plus quote plus the-guard.kind plus quote))
    end switch
end paragraph


!!! --- HTTP/1.1 requires a Host, and a request without one cannot be routed
!!! to a virtual host or safely used to build an absolute URL.

require-host receives request as http-request returns guard-result begin paragraph
    when (host-of with request being request) equals "" then
        give stopped-with with response being (error-response with code being status-bad-request,
            explanation being "HTTP/1.1 requires a Host header")
    end when
    give carry-on with nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Refuse a body past a ceiling, before a handler parses it.

body-limit receives request as http-request, setting as text returns guard-result begin paragraph
    value ceiling is nil.std.core::text_to_i32 with `value` being setting
    when (body-length with request being request) is greater than ceiling then
        give stopped-with with response being (error-response with code being status-payload-too-large,
            explanation being "The body is larger than this route accepts")
    end when
    give carry-on with nothing
end paragraph


require-form receives request as http-request returns guard-result begin paragraph
    value verb is method-name with verb being request.verb
    value writes is verb equals "POST" or verb equals "PUT" or verb equals "PATCH"
    when writes and not (is-form-encoded with request being request) then
        give stopped-with with response being (error-response with code being status-unsupported-media-type,
            explanation being "Send application/x-www-form-urlencoded")
    end when
    give carry-on with nothing
end paragraph


block-method receives request as http-request, setting as text returns guard-result begin paragraph
    when (method-name with verb being request.verb) equals (nil.std.text::to_upper with s being setting) then
        give stopped-with with response being (error-response with code being status-method-not-allowed,
            explanation being "That method is not accepted here")
    end when
    give carry-on with nothing
end paragraph


stopped-with receives response as http-response returns guard-result begin paragraph
    give build guard-result with stopped being true, response being response
end paragraph


carry-on returns guard-result begin paragraph
    give build guard-result with stopped being false, response being (empty-response with code being status-ok)
end paragraph


!!! --- Apply every finisher to the response, in order.

public run-finishers receives one-chain as chain, response as http-response returns http-response begin paragraph
    variable out is response
    repeat for each each-finisher in one-chain.finishers
        set out to run-one-finisher with the-finisher being each-finisher, response being out
    end repeat
    give out
end paragraph


run-one-finisher receives the-finisher as finisher, response as http-response returns http-response begin paragraph
    give switch the-finisher.kind
        case "server-name" then
            stop switching with (with-header with response being response, name being "Server",
                content being the-finisher.setting)
        case "security-headers" then
            stop switching with (security-headers with response being response)
        case "cache-control" then
            stop switching with (with-header with response being response, name being "Cache-Control",
                content being the-finisher.setting)
        case "allow-origin" then
            stop switching with (with-header with response being response,
                name being "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", content being the-finisher.setting)
        case "header" then
            stop switching with (named-header with response being response, setting being the-finisher.setting)
        otherwise
            !!! Unlike a guard, an unknown finisher leaves the response alone.
            !!! A missing header is a weaker outcome than a 500 on every page.
            stop switching with response
    end switch
end paragraph


!!! --- The headers worth setting on every response.
!!!
!!! nosniff stops a browser second-guessing the Content-Type that
!!! nilweb.static.files was careful about. DENY stops the page being framed,
!!! which is clickjacking. no-referrer-when-downgrade keeps the path out of
!!! the Referer sent to a plain-HTTP third party. None of them replace a
!!! Content-Security-Policy, which is the application's to write because only
!!! the application knows what it loads.

security-headers receives response as http-response returns http-response begin paragraph
    variable out is response
    set out to with-header with response being out, name being "X-Content-Type-Options", content being "nosniff"
    set out to with-header with response being out, name being "X-Frame-Options", content being "DENY"
    set out to with-header with response being out, name being "Referrer-Policy",
        content being "no-referrer-when-downgrade"
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- An arbitrary header, spelled "Name: value" in the setting.

named-header receives response as http-response, setting as text returns http-response begin paragraph
    value name is nil.std.text::trim with s being (before-first with input being setting, separator being ":")
    value content is nil.std.text::trim with s being (after-first with input being setting, separator being ":")
    when name equals "" then
        give response
    end when
    give with-header with response being response, name being name, content being content
end paragraph
